==============================================================================
  [3]  CONSISTENCY TEST  (Zhang Eq. 13)
==============================================================================

  F = (observed - predicted) / (2 x experimental uncertainty).
  |F| > 1 means that data point cannot be reconciled with the model.
  The Cantera column is the one to judge on: it uses the full model
  rather than the surrogate, so it is not affected by surrogate error.

